WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:07.409
I'm starting in the right atrium. Blood that is low in oxygen comes in here from the body.

00:00:07.659 --> 00:00:11.991
It passes through the tricuspid valve into the right ventricle.

00:00:12.241 --> 00:00:18.280
The right ventricle pumps it through the pulmonary valve to the lungs, where it picks up oxygen.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:26.553
Now it is high in oxygen, so I'm switching to red. It comes back through the pulmonary veins to the left atrium.

00:00:26.803 --> 00:00:30.495
It goes through the mitral valve into the left ventricle.

00:00:30.745 --> 00:00:36.954
Then the left ventricle pumps it through the aortic valve into the aorta, and out to the body.
